---
id: air-grilled-rainbow-trout
title: Air-Grilled Rainbow Trout Fillet
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 1
  cooked_g: 195

storage:
  fridge_days: 2
  freezer_friendly: true

equipment:
  - air-fryer
  - meat-thermometer
---

Pat @rainbow-trout-fillet{1} completely dry on both sides with paper towels, especially the skin.

Lightly brush the skin side with @avocado-oil{0.5%tsp} to prevent sticking to the basket and ensure a crisp texture. Season the flesh side evenly with @kosher-salt{0.25%tsp}, @black-pepper{0.25%tsp}, @garlic-powder{0.25%tsp}, and @smoked-paprika{0.25%tsp}.

Preheat #air-fryer to 200°C (400°F). Place the seasoned fillet skin-side down in the basket without flipping. Cook for ~air-fry-time{6%min}, checking at the 5-minute mark.

Pull the fillet when internal temperature reaches 55°C to 57°C (130°F–135°F) at the thickest part checked with a #meat-thermometer (the flesh should be opaque and flake under gentle fork pressure; do not exceed 60°C/140°F to prevent moisture loss and albumin curds).

Let rest for ~rest-time{2%min}, then transfer the fillet (195 g cooked) into a meal prep container.
